== Notes ==
* Baubles can be used at [[Shopkeeper]]s inside the Super Adventure Box to purchase [[List of Super Adventure Box upgrades and skills|items and upgrades]]. Baubles can also be used to buy [[Bauble Bubble]]s from [[Moto]] in [[Rata Sum]], which can then be used to purchase other items from him.
* While players are restricted with how many baubles they can collect while playing inside the Super Adventure Box (initial maximum of 250 baubles, with upgrades of 500, 750 and 1,000 respectively), there is no restriction outside other than inventory space.
* In tribulation mode, once the [[Cage]] is destroyed, additional baubles will appear around the end chest. Four [[50 Bauble]]s and six of either [[5 Bauble]]s (Zones 1-1, 2-1 and 2-2) or [[10 Bauble]]s (Zone 1-2) appear in an alternating pattern. This does not happen after defeating [[King Toad]] or [[Storm Wizard]].

== Trivia ==
* This is a reference to the rupee currency in [[w:The Legend of Zelda|The Legend of Zelda]] series.
* During the April 1, 2013, baubles were obtainable from [[Super Mysterious Chest]], that spawned in random places of the world.

